# importa-wasm — carrier-typed package-aware Wasm proof fixture (U6-D).
#
# Mirrors the `importa/importa.fab` sibling-import shape (entry + auxilium
# helper) with a CARRIER-TYPED cross-module call: `saluta(numerus) → numerus`.
#
# Why carrier-typed (recorded deviation from the textus `Salve, Marcus!`
# oracle): the product host instantiates each package module with its own
# linear memory, and the emitter's per-module literal table interns text rows
# into the shared host arena in module order — so a textus HANDLE passed from
# the entry into a sibling (or returned back) does not resolve today. A
# numerus carrier crosses the module boundary as a plain i64, which the host
# `faber_external` symbol binding resolves (the U6-E carrier proof: 41 → 42 →
# stdout). The textus-handle limitation is a recorded residual of this unit.
#
# The import uses the grammar-native `importa ex` form (the corpus `import
# from` spelling is the keyword-exemplum frontmatter alias, which needs the
# `aliases` frontmatter to lex).
#
# EXPECTED OUTPUT:
#   "42" on successful package link + run through the product host.

importa ex "./auxilium" privata auxilium

main {
    print auxilium.saluta(41)
}
